  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2025-2026 Arkansas Tech University Catalog, 'Organizational Leadership Child Development Option, Bachelor of Arts' curriculum (pp. 308-310), a genuine institution-published semester sequence, offered 100% online. Footnote 2: at least 40 of the total hours required for graduation must be 3000-4000 level courses. Footnote 3: a grade of 'C' or better required (marked courses). Footnote 4: 18 credit hours of Organizational Leadership electives are required from: BAS 4253 Quality Control, BAS 4353 Project Management, BAS 4363 Project Risk Analysis and Mitigation, BAS 4373 Leading Agile Projects, BAS 4453 Root Cause Analysis, BAS 4553 Occupational Safety, LEAD 4003 Leadership Internship/Capstone Seminar, LEAD 4103 Special Problems in Leadership, OL 3233 Volunteer Leadership and Development, OL 4053 Philanthropy and Fundraising, OL 4143 Nonprofit Organizations, OL 4243 Adult Learning in Organizations, OL 4343 Community Development, OL 4743 Organizational Change, OL 4843 Training and Organizational Development, and/or OL 4993 Special Problems in Organizational Leadership — seeded as choice slots with code 'OL ELECTIVE'. Select-one slots printed: 'LEAD 1003 Introduction to Leadership or LEAD 3003 Leading Teams' (sophomore spring), 'NUR 2303 Nutrition or HA 2813 Basic Human Nutrition in Hospitality Administration' (senior fall), and 'OL 4043 Ethical Decision-Making and Development or LEAD 2003 Ethics in Leadership' (senior spring), seeded as choice slots with options. The program partners the BA with the MA Organizational Leadership and Learning: a maximum of twelve graduate-level credit hours (any 5000-6000 level OL course except OL 6093 Organizational Development and Learning Capstone) can count toward both degrees — noted here in notes only, never seeded as machine options. Machine prereqs omitted (prereq: []) — the curriculum page prints no per-course prerequisites. tccns mirrors the local ATU course